{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The coveted.</b> Fine and new garments in which he honors himself before people and serves his father in them — and therefore Isaac smelled them, for new garments give off the scent of the dye. Another interpretation: <b>the coveted</b> — that he would wear them when he went out to the field to hunt game, and they would give off the scent of the field and the trees, as it is written, \"And he smelled the scent of his garments and said etc.\" like the scent of the field; and that day Esau had not worn them when he went to hunt game." "<b>The coveted.</b> We find garments in the feminine form: ובגדיו לא תשרפנה — 'and his garments you shall not burn' (feminine plural)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:15.795765659Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}